From: mothershipOS
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: prepare the DisplayPort codec before the Q6 AFE port

q6afe-dai starts the DSP's DISPLAY_PORT_RX port in its prepare, and the DSP only accepts that once the DP
controller's audio engine runs. The msm DP driver turns the engine on in its codec prepare (drm_hdmi_audio_helper),
which ASoC calls after the CPU DAI's: the port start timed out (-110) and left the port unusable (DSP error 9)
until the card was reloaded. The link prepare runs first: prepare the codec DAIs there for DISPLAY_PORT_RX.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -150,6 +150,23 @@
 	struct sm8250_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
 	struct sdw_stream_runtime *sruntime = data->sruntime[cpu_dai->id];
 
+	/*
+	 * DisplayPort: the DSP's AFE port only starts (q6afe-dai prepare) once the DP controller's audio engine runs,
+	 * and the DP driver turns that on in its codec prepare, which ASoC calls after the CPU DAI's: the port start
+	 * times out (-110). Prepare the codec first; its own prepare later reprograms the same, idle, engine.
+	 */
+	if (cpu_dai->id == DISPLAY_PORT_RX) {
+		struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai;
+		int i, ret;
+
+		for_each_rtd_codec_dais(rtd, i, codec_dai) {
+			ret = snd_soc_dai_prepare(codec_dai, substream);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				return ret;
+		}
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	return qcom_snd_sdw_prepare(substream, sruntime,
 				    &data->stream_prepared[cpu_dai->id]);
 }
